   "text": {
    "L1": "A play has speakers and actions. Read only the spoken words in your role.",
    "L2": "Words in brackets tell you what to do or how to speak. Do not read them aloud.",
    "L3": "In Lagori, one team knocks down a pile of stones and rebuilds it.",
    "L4": "The other team tries to hit the players with the ball while they rebuild.",
    "L5": "The team won because each child had a job and they worked together.",
    "L6": "Excitement sounds fast and bright. Read an exclamation with energy.",
    "L7": "A question rises at the end, as in, 'What are you doing?'",
    "L8": "For a suggestion, use Let's and a plain action word: 'Let's play!'"
